course: dictionary
lesson: 10766
title: Usual and as usual
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Usual means what normally happens, or what is done most of the time. The usual bus is the bus you catch every day. When you read «When Lily's usual friends fall out and leave her alone, Sam sits with her at lunch», the word usual tells you who Lily normally spends time with.
explain: As usual means in the same way as always. «As usual» tells the reader that something is a habit. If a story says the dog barked at the postman, as usual, you know this happens every day. Look for «as usual» to spot routines.
explain: Usual can compare too. «Eastern tree frogs in the zone are darker than usual» means they are darker than their normal colour. Than usual always compares something with the normal amount. Unusual is the opposite: it means something strange, and it may matter to the plot of a story.
fact: Usual means what normally happens or what is done most of the time.
fact: As usual means in the same way as always.
fact: «Than usual» compares something with the normal amount, as in «colder than usual».
fact: «Unusual» means not normal, so it often shows that something strange might matter.
fact: Phrases to learn: as usual, than usual, the usual, business as usual.
exercise: «When Lily's usual friends fall out and leave her alone, Sam sits with her at lunch.» What does usual mean here? | Friends who are kind to dogs | Friends from a faraway country | Friends she has just met | *The friends Lily normally has
exercise: Spanish scientists say eastern tree frogs are «darker than usual». What does this compare? | How loudly the frogs sing | *The normal darkness of these frogs | How fast the frogs swim | The colour of the sky
exercise: «Mum is late again, as usual.» What does as usual mean? | Only on Sundays | *In the same way as always | For the first time ever | In a new and surprising way
test: «The usual suspect is a guess, not proof.» What does this tell you about the usual suspect? | A suspect who was never seen | A suspect the police have proved guilty | *Someone people normally blame, but it is not proof | A famous detective
test: Each kind of living thing has its own usual length of life. About how many years is a dog's usual life? | *About ten to fifteen | About two or three | About five thousand | About seventy
exam: Which phrase means in the same way as always? | Unusual | The usual | *As usual | Than usual
